**Definition 1.3 (raw record and finite slot catalog).** Let $W(h)$ contain
the 74 actual finite tape words in port order, with all eight tracks,
including boundary, head, seal, reserved and meter tracks; every constructed
finite control location, active and inactive code stores, PC, mode, cursor,
phase, latches and tokens; and the fixed source/port binding. A cell's
physical identity is its port and creation-chain position, as in ARC
Definition 6.2. Encoded origin references are their actual tape material.
An interpretation such as an event list or current tree is not an extra
physical store. Absolute construction-event provenance is carried by the
actual execution relation; it is not inferred from an unnamed tree shape.

Enumerate the possible finite physical locations once by physical identity:
primitive fields, original boot/control version, capture $L$, expanded $G$,
and their actual fixed bootstrap/phase/token/cursor fields, in that order
and then their owning field/bit order. Reused locations are listed once;
retained distinct versions are distinct. Let the catalog have size $q\ge1$.
Its entries have values absent, 0 or 1. A dynamic table on 24, a captured
description, simulated code, natural, bank field or descriptor is ordinary
tape data, not an extra finite location. The catalog and all fixed native
store lengths depend on this initially chosen finite apparatus, never on
future $J$, a later word length or an elapsed ordinal.

